From 35525654e8a3c43f6e49ad0562aa2025c38e5e81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:17:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: histb-vdec bring-up bench

Restore the bring-up bench for the decoder block on top of the submitted
series: the debugfs pool window, the forced-VP8 lever and the live A/B
parameters whose board question is still open.

For the HEVC arm the settled bits are already folded into the submitted
code and stay folded here: BIT(9) (PRC_CACHE_TYPE=2 as the vendor
writes), BIT(10) (the HEVC timeout constant), BIT(15) (the CTB-grid pad
behind the single-CTB-row refusal), BIT(16)/BIT(17) (the tile acceptance
probe the E16 board question needs). For MPEG-2: BIT(0) (MPEG-1 sequence
reading), BIT(3)/BIT(4)/BIT(6) (the SCD select-reset pulse, SCD_EMAR_ID
bit16 and the wider interrupt mask, all still differing from the vendor
firmware), and BIT(7)..BIT(11).

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
